#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:9
msgid "What I do"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:11
msgid ""
"Provide actionable guidance for planning and executing migrations safely."
" Every migration — schema, data, API, or library — must have a tested "
"rollback path, a monitoring plan, and a strategy that avoids downtime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:13
msgid "When to use me"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:15
msgid ""
"Load this skill when planning or executing any migration: database schema"
" changes, data transformations, API version transitions, or library "
"upgrades. The migration-engineer and platform-delivery-lead should load "
"this before writing or reviewing a migration spec."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:17
msgid "Core principle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:19
msgid ""
"Every migration is a contract with production. You are changing something"
" that running systems depend on. The cost of a failed migration is not "
"\"we fix it tomorrow\" — it's data loss, broken clients, or extended "
"downtime. Plan accordingly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:21
msgid "Zero-downtime migration techniques"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:23
msgid "Expand-contract (preferred for most migrations)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:25
msgid "The safest general-purpose pattern. Three phases:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:27
msgid ""
"**Expand**: Add the new structure alongside the old one. Both coexist. "
"Old code continues to work unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:28
msgid ""
"**Migrate**: Move data/traffic/consumers to the new structure. Verify "
"correctness."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:29
msgid ""
"**Contract**: Remove the old structure after all consumers have migrated "
"and a soak period has passed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:31
msgid ""
"Never collapse these into one step. The expand phase is your safety net —"
" if anything goes wrong during migration, you still have the old "
"structure intact."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:33
msgid "Blue-green"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:35
msgid ""
"Run two complete environments in parallel. Route traffic to the new "
"environment after verification. Keep the old environment warm for instant"
" rollback."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:37
msgid "Use blue-green when:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:38
msgid "The migration involves infrastructure changes, not just code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:39
msgid "You need to verify the entire stack, not just individual components"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:40
msgid "Rollback must be instantaneous (seconds, not minutes)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:42
msgid "Feature flags"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:44
msgid ""
"Gate new behavior behind a flag. Roll out gradually — 1%, 10%, 50%, 100%."
" Monitor error rates at each stage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:46
msgid "Use feature flags when:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:47
msgid ""
"The migration is behavioral (new logic, new data flow) rather than "
"structural (new schema)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:48
msgid "You want to decouple deployment from activation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:49
msgid "You need per-user or per-tenant rollout control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:51
msgid "Database migration safety"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:53
msgid "Backwards-compatible schema changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:55
msgid ""
"Every schema migration must be backwards-compatible with the currently "
"deployed application code. The deployment sequence is: deploy schema "
"change, then deploy application code. If the schema change breaks "
"existing code, you have a window of failure between the two deployments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:57
msgid "**Safe operations:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:58
msgid "Add a nullable column"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:59
msgid "Add a new table"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:60
msgid ""
"Add an index (use `CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY` on PostgreSQL to avoid "
"locks)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:61
msgid "Widen a column type (e.g., `VARCHAR(50)` to `VARCHAR(100)`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:63
msgid "**Unsafe operations (require expand-contract):**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:64
msgid ""
"Rename a column — instead, add new column, backfill, update code, drop "
"old column"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:65
msgid ""
"Remove a column — instead, stop reading it in code, deploy, then drop it "
"in a later migration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:66
msgid "Change a column type to something narrower or incompatible"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:67
msgid ""
"Add a NOT NULL constraint to an existing column — instead, add a CHECK "
"constraint first, backfill nulls, then add NOT NULL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:68
msgid "Drop a table that any code still references"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:70
msgid "Rollback strategies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:72
msgid ""
"Every migration script must have a corresponding rollback script. Test "
"the rollback on a copy of production data before running the forward "
"migration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:74
msgid ""
"**Additive migrations** (add column, add table): Rollback is dropping the"
" addition. Simple but verify no code depends on it yet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:75
msgid ""
"**Data migrations** (backfill, transform): Rollback requires preserving "
"the original data. Either keep the old column until the migration is "
"confirmed, or take a logical backup of affected rows before transforming."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:76
msgid ""
"**Destructive migrations** (drop column, drop table): These are "
"irreversible. Only execute after a soak period confirms nothing depends "
"on the dropped structure. Always take a backup immediately before."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:78
msgid "Lock management"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:80
msgid ""
"Long-running migrations on large tables can acquire locks that block "
"reads/writes. Mitigate this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:81
msgid ""
"Use online DDL tools (`pt-online-schema-change` for MySQL, `pg_repack` "
"for PostgreSQL) for large table alterations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:82
msgid ""
"Set statement timeouts on migration connections so a stuck migration "
"doesn't hold locks indefinitely"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:83
msgid "Schedule lock-acquiring migrations during low-traffic windows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:84
msgid "Monitor lock wait times during execution"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:86
msgid "Data transformation patterns"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:88
msgid "Batch processing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:90
msgid "Never transform all rows in a single transaction. Process in batches:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:91
msgid "Choose a batch size that completes in under 1 second per batch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:92
msgid "Commit after each batch to release locks and allow checkpointing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:93
msgid ""
"Track progress (last processed ID or timestamp) so the job can resume "
"after interruption"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:94
msgid "Add a configurable sleep between batches to reduce load on the database"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:96
msgid "Idempotent transforms"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:98
msgid ""
"Every data transformation must be safe to run multiple times. If the job "
"crashes at batch 5,000 and restarts from batch 4,900, the overlapping "
"rows must not be corrupted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:100
msgid "Design for idempotency:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:101
msgid "Use `INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE` instead of blind inserts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:102
msgid "Guard updates with a condition: `UPDATE ... WHERE status != 'migrated'`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:103
msgid "Use a migration status column or tracking table to mark processed rows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:105
msgid "Validation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:107
msgid "Before, during, and after:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:108
msgid "**Before**: Count rows, sample data, verify assumptions about data shape"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:109
msgid ""
"**During**: Log batch progress, error counts, and skipped rows. Stop on "
"unexpected error rates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:110
msgid ""
"**After**: Run validation queries comparing old and new data. Verify row "
"counts match. Spot-check edge cases (nulls, empty strings, extreme "
"values, unicode)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:112
msgid "API version migration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:114
msgid "Parallel running"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:116
msgid "When migrating an API version:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:117
msgid ""
"Deploy the new version alongside the old one (e.g., `/v2/users` alongside"
" `/v1/users`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:118
msgid "Route new consumers to v2. Existing consumers stay on v1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:119
msgid "Monitor both versions. Compare response shapes, error rates, latency."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:120
msgid "Set a deprecation date for v1. Communicate it to consumers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:121
msgid "After all consumers have migrated, remove v1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:123
msgid "Consumer coordination"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:125
msgid ""
"Identify all consumers before starting. Check API keys, access logs, "
"documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:126
msgid ""
"Notify consumers with a concrete timeline: \"v1 will stop accepting "
"requests on [date].\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:127
msgid ""
"Provide a migration guide showing the v1-to-v2 mapping for every endpoint"
" and field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:128
msgid ""
"Monitor v1 traffic. Do not remove v1 until traffic reaches zero or the "
"deprecation deadline passes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:130
msgid "Deprecation timelines"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:132
msgid ""
"Internal APIs: minimum 2 sprint cycles between deprecation notice and "
"removal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:133
msgid "External APIs: minimum 3 months, preferably 6"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:134
msgid ""
"Add deprecation headers (`Deprecation`, `Sunset`) to v1 responses during "
"the transition"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:136
msgid "Library upgrade strategies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:138
msgid "Incremental upgrades"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:140
msgid ""
"Never skip major versions. If you're on v2 and need v5, upgrade "
"v2→v3→v4→v5 sequentially. Each step should be a separate commit with "
"passing tests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:142
msgid "Adapter patterns"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:144
msgid ""
"When a library's API changes significantly between versions, introduce an"
" adapter layer:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:145
msgid "Create a thin wrapper around the current library usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:146
msgid "Migrate all call sites to use the wrapper"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:147
msgid "Swap the wrapper's internals to the new library version"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:148
msgid "Remove the wrapper once the new API is stable and well-understood"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:150
msgid "Compatibility shims"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:152
msgid "For breaking changes in function signatures or behavior:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:153
msgid "Write shim functions that translate old call patterns to new ones"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:154
msgid "Mark shims with `@deprecated` or equivalent so they get cleaned up"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:155
msgid ""
"Set a deadline for removing shims — they are temporary bridges, not "
"permanent fixtures"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:157
msgid "Rollback planning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:159
msgid ""
"**Every migration must have a documented rollback plan.** This is non-"
"negotiable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:161
msgid "The rollback plan must answer:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:162
msgid ""
"**Trigger**: What conditions indicate the migration has failed? (error "
"rate spike, data inconsistency, consumer complaints)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:163
msgid ""
"**Procedure**: Step-by-step instructions to revert. No \"undo the "
"migration\" hand-waving — specific commands, scripts, or deployment "
"steps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:164
msgid ""
"**Data recovery**: If the migration transformed data, how do you restore "
"the original state?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:165
msgid ""
"**Timeline**: How long does the rollback take? Is it seconds (feature "
"flag), minutes (revert deployment), or hours (restore from backup)?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:166
msgid "**Verification**: How do you confirm the rollback succeeded?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:168
msgid ""
"Test the rollback before running the migration. If you can't test it, "
"you're not ready to migrate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:170
msgid "Monitoring during migration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:172
msgid "What to watch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:174
msgid ""
"**Error rates**: Both application errors and database errors. Compare to "
"baseline."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:175
msgid ""
"**Latency**: P50, P95, P99. Migrations that add load can spike tail "
"latency."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:176
msgid "**Lock waits**: Database lock wait times and deadlock counts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:177
msgid ""
"**Queue depths**: If the migration generates async work, watch queue "
"backlogs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:178
msgid ""
"**Consumer health**: If migrating an API, monitor downstream consumer "
"error rates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:179
msgid ""
"**Disk space**: Data migrations can temporarily double storage "
"requirements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:181
msgid "When to abort"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:183
msgid "Abort the migration if:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:184
msgid "Error rate exceeds 2x baseline for more than 5 minutes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:185
msgid "P99 latency exceeds 3x baseline"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:186
msgid "Any deadlock that isn't automatically resolved"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:187
msgid "Data validation checks fail on a sample batch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:188
msgid "Disk usage approaches capacity limits"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/migration-safety/SKILL.md:190
msgid ""
"Aborting is not failure — it's professionalism. A migration that's "
"aborted and retried after investigation is far better than one that's "
"pushed through and causes an incident."
msgstr ""

